{%- comment -%}
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CUSTOMER OWNS PLAYER (age collection template + basket prompt)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Outputs "true" when the signed-in customer has bought something with a player in it, otherwise nothing. Use it with
capture:  {%- capture owns_player -%}{%- render 'customer-owns-player' -%}{%- endcapture -%}

"Has a player in it" = product type Player, Starter Pack or Schools Pack, or the tag "Player Bundle".
Only signed-in customers can be recognised here; everyone else is treated as new (the basket prompt also remembers
"I already have a player" in the browser, see voxblock.js).
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign owns = false
  if customer
    for order in customer.orders
      for item in order.line_items
        assign item_type = item.product.type | downcase
        if item_type == 'player' or item_type == 'starter pack' or item_type == 'schools pack' or item.product.tags contains 'Player Bundle'
          assign owns = true
          break
        endif
      endfor
      if owns
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif
  if owns
    echo 'true'
  endif
-%}
